Context: T146. Design choices: in-package (internal/hubsync) so the benches reuse appendRecordSection and the production batchEncoder/batchDecoder (CRC on, WithDecodeAllCapLimit); klauspost exposes four speed classes, not the zstd level range, so rows are labeled by class (fastest/default/better/best) - a 'level 5' bench is identical to 3; the decode bench decodes into per-stream buffers sized like the production rawLen allocation because the cap limit bounds decode at the destination capacity. Fixture corpus is one lazy sync.OnceValue per process; x-ratio is N-independent so benchstat compares it directly.
